@startuml GitHub OAuth — Loopback Flow

title GitHub OAuth (Loopback / RFC 8252)

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #f5f5f5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #aaaaaa
skinparam noteBorderColor #aaaaaa
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fffde7

actor User

box "App (common)" #e8f5e9
  participant "LoginViewModel" as VM
end box

box "App (platform)" #e3f2fd
  participant "GithubOAuthLauncher" as Launcher
  participant "LocalHttpServer\n(127.0.0.1:PORT)" as Server
  participant "In-App Browser\n(CCT / SFSafariVC)" as Browser
end box

box "External" #fce4ec
  participant "GitHub OAuth" as GitHub
  participant "Taiga API" as API
end box

== Initiation ==

User -> VM : tap "Continue with GitHub"
VM -> API : GET /conf.json
API --> VM : { gitHubClientId }
VM -> Launcher : launch(baseAuthUrl)

== Loopback Setup ==

Launcher -> Server : start on random free port
note right of Server
  ServerSocket(0) gives OS-assigned port.
  GitHub allows http://127.0.0.1 without registration.
end note

Launcher -> Browser : open\nhttps://github.com/login/oauth/authorize\n?client_id=...&redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:PORT/callback\n&state=github&scope=user:email

== User Authentication ==

User -> Browser : authenticate on GitHub
GitHub -> Server : GET /callback?code=XXX&state=github
Server --> GitHub : 200 OK (close this tab)

== Code Handoff ==

Server --> Launcher : code = "XXX"
Launcher -> Browser : close / bring app to foreground
Launcher --> VM : return code

== Token Exchange ==

VM -> API : POST /api/v1/auth\n{ type: "github", code: "XXX" }
note right
  Taiga backend calls GitHub directly
  with client_secret to exchange code.
  redirect_uri is NOT sent — no validation.
end note
API --> VM : { auth_token, refresh, id }
VM -> VM : store credentials
VM --> User : navigate to projects

@enduml